@node Surface Class
@section §11.0.1 — The Surface Class

New in Steelbore 2. Surface tokens carry the following hard rules:

@itemize
@item
Surface tokens are @strong{never text colors}. Quantum Blue is 1.40:1
and Deep Matrix 1.14:1 against Void Navy --- both are illegible as
foregrounds anywhere.
@item
A surface's edge against the canvas (1.40:1 / 1.14:1) does not meet the
3:1 non-text floor. Where the boundary is meaningful, it @strong{must}
be drawn --- a Pulse Violet border (5.51:1 vs canvas) is the canonical
edge.
@item
Surfaces never nest on each other without a measured boundary.
@end itemize

@node Contrast Guarantee
@section §11.0.2 — Scope of the Contrast Guarantee

Every foreground token is verified with the WCAG relative-luminance
formula against all three backgrounds it may legally appear on. AA
floors: @strong{4.5:1} normal text (1.4.3); @strong{3:1} large text and
non-text UI (1.4.3, 1.4.11). EN 301 549 V4.1.1 clause 11 (11.1.4.3,
11.1.4.11) inherits the same criteria for non-web software; the EAA has
been enforceable since 2025-06-28.

@multitable {Plasma Magenta} {vs Void Navy} {vs Quantum Blue} {vs Deep Matrix}
@headitem
Foreground
